Draft one workflow using ONLY these complete real contracts and the approved 17-type palette: branch_node, check_reply_node, concat_node, conditional_node, context_pack_node, end_node, file_output_node, file_reader_node, find_lines_node, json_path_node, merge_node, read_lines_node, start_node, text_output_node, text_transform_node, user_text_input_node, wait_until_node. Return one JSON object, no Markdown, at most 8,000 characters. Format aotn-workflow/1, name, nodes (handle -> type, alias/config), connections (from/to handle.port). Start and End required. Handles are lowercase identifiers, ports are literal machine ids. Ordinary outputs follow only their FIRST wire; parallel work needs branch_node with real path_a/path_b. To use parallel results together: one branch_node, each path wired to its own merge_node input (reader_a.default to join.path_a, reader_b.default to join.path_b), then join.default to the next step. For more than two paths set branch_count on the branch_node: 3 gives path_a, path_b and path_c, and so on up to 64. Merge has inputs path_a to path_e unless input_slots raises it. Merge passes on one record keyed by input name, so that step reads {{input[path_a]}} and {{input[path_b]}}. A path may split again, and its children join the same Merge: gather.default to inner.input, inner.path_a to upper.input, upper.default to join.path_b, lower.default to join.path_c; the inner branch_node needs no Merge input. Either-or routes may share one input: choose.true to yes.input, choose.false to no.input, yes.default and no.default both to join.path_b; that input holds the one that ran, and every route must reach the Merge. Concurrent paths in one input give a list in path order, read as {{input[path_b][0]}}; prefer separate inputs. To hold one path until a step on another finishes, put wait_until_node first on the waiting path with target_node_ids set to the handle of that step, ["read"], never the branch_node; it passes on its own input, not that step's value. A text_output_node passes on its text with its label in front, so one feeding a Merge needs "label": "". A split and its sub-paths use only one Merge. No loops. A Merge needs a split, and join.default must feed a step before End. A path may end on its own only if it supplies nothing the request needs. A shared End only finishes each path; it never waits for or combines them. Conditional equals compares strings; route true/false correctly. Respect ACTIVE source fields, raw content and requested paths. Write Create unique unless otherwise explicitly allowed; no automatic opening. Show actual returned File Reference path via {{input[path]}} or JSON Path(path) then {{input}}, never guessed basename or dict repr. In FINAL Text Output templates use SINGLE Python braces, not doubled braces. No model/network/shell/deletion/integration effects. No assumptions hiding missing requirements. A structural check is not proof of meaning or permission to execute. Example wire: {{"from":"start.default","to":"show.input"}}. Use only machine port id after the dot; display names are labels.

